  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<p>This dashboard contains details of animal samples that tested positive for rabies in Manitoba since the province took over the rabies program on April 1, 2014. As of April 1, 2014 the Canadian Food Inspection Agency (CFIA) is no longer involved in managing rabies cases in Manitoba. <span style='font-size:medium;'><font style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>The provincial Rabies Management Program is now coordinated by&nbsp;</font></span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' target='_blank' href='https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/animal-health-and-welfare/animal-health/rabies.html' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:medium;'><font style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Manitoba Rabies Central</font></span></a><span style='font-size:medium;'><font style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>, which is a collaborative effort involving the Manitoba departments of Health, Seniors and Long-Term Care, Agriculture, and Natural Resources and Indigenous Futures. Samples for rabies testing are requested by Manitoba Health, Seniors and Long-Term Care in the case of exposure of a human to a suspected rabid animal and by Agriculture in the case of exposure of another animal to a suspect rabid animal. Collection of a sample from the suspect rabid animal is coordinated by Manitoba Agriculture.</font></span></p><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><span style='font-size:medium;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'>This information will be updated on a quarterly basis.</font></span></div>"
